{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/changelog.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731599Z","id":"1fb89fe2180e9ab019630a1a78c0b9f76ee918b2667200528bf8b5c7849a2206","body":{"detail":"Seen 2026-10-05 at load 20 to 35 at line 43; passed on rerun. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"d93e69430a460d0d729b834fd1892c1d2bfcc9d9a0ba9ac58cddbe3f0eddb23b"},"summary":".thread-pin.addressed not found within 5 s under load","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183659Z","id":"067e86b131a6604c662a4ddc88c5bbc8fb80134b3435996a6131e758c86fa1b9","body":{"detail":"This test checks that a publish reaches all 14 interested tabs within expect's 5 s timeout and logs the latencies; its former 500 ms bound was removed because wall-clock budgets in functional tests fail under load. The time-to-usable perf gate (web/perf) measures a tab's first paint and comment readiness, and scripts/perf-clients.py measures delivery to raw /api/stream clients, so delivery through the shared-worker hub to tabs is judged by no machine-scaled budget.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":279},"end":{"line":280},"content_hash":"88bb3bff31f4a493c95de0da980670497784345a77df890009cf86b3b9389241"},"suggested_fix":"Add a publish-to-tab delivery measure to the time-to-usable perf gate, scaled by its control like its other measures.","summary":"No gate judges how fast a publish reaches open tabs","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:37:53.331008Z","id":"f222d027b2d6d615342a7bb566e8c4f72d207528e46980c8bc4af53dab32355a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7165f70","summary":"The thirty-tab test no longer judges wall-clock budgets: it asserts the daemon opened no stream for the new tabs or the publish (streams opened, from /api/_test/stream/open), that other artifacts' tabs neither heard the publish nor went live again, and that the publish reaches all 14 interested tabs within expect's timeout; times are logged only. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts 'thirty tabs share one stream; a new tab joins it, and a publish reaches every tab that wants it and no other' passes 3 of 3 runs (npx playwright test e2e/streams.spec.ts --project rest --repeat-each 3: 39 passed), and passed 24 of 24 runs beside four busy loops with new tabs taking up to 1741 ms.","supersedes":"980f4257b517a4f9de109de736d0da13aeeec4707cdbb942f508fc48af2a2b40","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:37:53.379068Z","id":"15eb52d946d3f4d01c78610de84ec28e068b72544a9b9d0970b97e02d438d36e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9a85e31","summary":"Cause: one rename was announced several times (the PUT and the presence event), and each tab reopened the shared stream for each; a stream request aborted before it answers stays open while Chrome drains it (about 5 s), so the daemon held two admin streams meanwhile. The hub now reopens only when the asked caller differs from the one the stream's ready names. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts: the owner's rename with 1, 2 or 3 tabs opens 0 streams and a LAN viewer's opens exactly 1 (3 of 3 runs each), and the late-token test opens exactly 1 stream at admin; web/shell/src/stream-hub.test.ts 'reopens once per caller however many tabs ask' passes.","supersedes":"76c0610dd30031ed20e78da3f4e5f68c716ab3b97145f2a17398ebb716e52514","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/hosted-demo-worker.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:49:03.385917Z","id":"acddd66722505cdb95b3eab866a7afdb8f2fadb62e1e960dfe592ce3e5d4bd77","body":{"detail":"It runs only with CLAX_E2E_WORKER=1 (about 30 s on a warm build), so scripts/quality_gates.sh never runs it; adding it to lane_e2e after `worker e2e` would grow the e2e lane past the suite's two-minute budget. BUILT checks only that crates/clax-worker/build/index.js and web/dist/index.html exist: the Worker embeds web/dist when built (crates/clax-server/src/routes/shell.rs, rust-embed), so a Worker built before the last scripts/build-web.sh serves entry pages naming the previous chunks, and a shell change is not what the check sees. A check could compare build/index_bg.wasm's mtime with web/node_modules/.clax-web-built's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"11223399ac5334b44d7d2280a3ecf4d98c25c24639e1002e78dedd0e168b76ee"},"summary":"The Worker demo check is not in the quality gates, and a Worker built before web/dist passes its built check while serving the old shell","tags":["demo","worker","tests","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815280Z","id":"31593a13b54c0dec306574773eeefbe84aa3e919a13e65688e6b66b626e23687","body":{"detail":"Failure: npx playwright test e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts (one worker, fresh worker daemon) fails at line 44 in both modes with author \"Alex (not connected)\" where \"Alex\" is expected. It passes in a full run, where other tests ran on the same worker daemon first. Reproduced with the a2378555 daemon and shell (built apart), so it predates the agent strip work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"f8ceff7f0a68a38fca7ca0904b2fbf782748a42e198f6039c02873a29a84e121"},"summary":"comment-loop.spec.ts fails when run alone: the author reads 'Alex (not connected)'","tags":["e2e","flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/people.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.891553Z","id":"4ab0a73e32e9ea8a5fa7517e8cbdb137ac1c1a921f0e23a9c55001c592b4ec52","body":{"detail":"Failure: npx playwright test e2e/people.spec.ts fails at line 73 (expected 'claude', received 'sam-notes'), 3 of 3 runs at 86cc3ac0 and with the e9d4941b daemon built apart, so it predates the delivery-state work. Joins now keep repository names (git:7c23e721), and scripts/dev-second-person.sh registers its agent from a scratch project '<name>-notes'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"65d11761c212fc5e95d9eeb36ff2d687143aa7efce7c3a0b6f49c707b14d0229"},"suggested_fix":"Expect the repository's name (sam-notes), as the agent strip's e2e does.","summary":"people.spec.ts expects a hook-registered agent named 'claude'; agents are now named after their repository ('sam-notes')","tags":["e2e","task:19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/people.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:22:49.499987Z","id":"a5fd2ef807338af799243003d21f9dd7eb43b4dcedf86d51f131c7bc9bdb553e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4ea835a5","summary":"Fixed by 4ea835a5 (Expect the people e2e's hook-registered agent to be named after its checkout): web/e2e/people.spec.ts now expects 'sam-notes', the agent a hook's join names after its checkout since it sends its repository (spec §11). Evidence: with CLAX_TEST_BIN from scripts/stable-bin.sh, npx playwright test e2e/people.spec.ts e2e/creator-raise.spec.ts e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts: 4 passed on the tree carried onto 4d499f5e.","supersedes":"4ab0a73e32e9ea8a5fa7517e8cbdb137ac1c1a921f0e23a9c55001c592b4ec52","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:37:51.768803Z","id":"e16e6e63b41be1d5dc09982f4658c5d7de55eddbe90e1ca7cf24fed6ab74c5fa","body":{"detail":"Seen on multi-person at 628b724a: npx playwright test e2e/whole-comment.spec.ts (run alone, CLAX_TEST_BIN set) fails at line 58, expect(fb.feedback[0]).toMatchObject({author: 'Alex', ...}) receiving 'Alex (not connected)'; comment-loop.spec.ts fails at line 44 as this record says. Neither spec touches delivery states, and both reach the card's 'sent, waiting for the agent' label as the owner before failing.","kind":"comment","references":"31593a13b54c0dec306574773eeefbe84aa3e919a13e65688e6b66b626e23687","summary":"web/e2e/whole-comment.spec.ts:58 fails the same way: the feedback item's author reads 'Alex (not connected)'","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271582Z","id":"fce385daee3e7fb1fe088f68e579b738c811d8532e6849c0c9e56c7f2eabc772","body":{"detail":"A product defect, not a test one: on a fresh daemon the test's agent reads (register, publish) before the owner's browser exists, Store::connected() caches a Connected with no owner, and the owner's later comments read 'Alex (not connected)' until the generation moves. Bumping it in owner_viewer makes both specs pass alone; main, which has no not-connected mark, passes both specs alone too.","kind":"comment","references":"31593a13b54c0dec306574773eeefbe84aa3e919a13e65688e6b66b626e23687","summary":"Cause found: Store::owner_viewer makes the owner's row without bumping the visibility generation (record on crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:540-557)","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.408021Z","id":"d43da47a0251d28c64b82f6f53b6894b2b8fa8bf4b10eeb7a52bd1ed82234e78","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c84e0d7a","summary":"Answered by record 0e7b9b6c: the owner's row was made without bumping the visibility generation, so an agent's earlier read cached a Connected with no owner. Fixed in c84e0d7a; comment-loop.spec.ts (2 passed) and whole-comment.spec.ts (1 passed) pass alone, and the full Playwright run passes (414 passed).","supersedes":"31593a13b54c0dec306574773eeefbe84aa3e919a13e65688e6b66b626e23687","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/people-helpers.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.547055Z","id":"7f91539a6249639e0185b6d89b36cfb73aef296d7b352fc6f8b453b2ee76838a","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts, inbox-cards.spec.ts, people.spec.ts, creator-raise.spec.ts and chrome-overlay.spec.ts strip only CLAX_CHANNEL, CLAUDECODE, CODEX_SESSION_ID and CLAX_PORT. Run under Claude Code, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID reaches their shims and hooks, which then register with the runner's harness session ID: harmless with one agent per person, but two shims of one person join one session (visibility.spec.ts hit it). personEnv here strips every CLAX_, CLAUDE*, CODEX_, GROK_ and PI_CODING_AGENT variable; those specs could import it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"ee354380d688ec043d58b7b4977126fb67df42e528c7c809e6bfd1101c8c4eb0"},"summary":"Other browser tests start person CLIs with the runner's harness variables","tags":["e2e","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/hosted-demo-worker.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"1a5cdcce390a1102487d142d40a3776fefaea7ef6529283576968f4568ad4367","body":{"detail":"It runs only with CLAX_E2E_WORKER=1 (about 30 s on a warm build), so scripts/quality_gates.sh never runs it; adding it to lane_e2e after `worker e2e` would grow the e2e lane past the suite's two-minute budget. BUILT checks only that crates/clax-worker/build/index.js and web/dist/index.html exist: the Worker embeds web/dist when built (crates/clax-server/src/routes/shell.rs, rust-embed), so a Worker built before the last scripts/build-web.sh serves entry pages naming the previous chunks, and a shell change is not what the check sees. A check could compare build/index_bg.wasm's mtime with web/node_modules/.clax-web-built's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"11223399ac5334b44d7d2280a3ecf4d98c25c24639e1002e78dedd0e168b76ee"},"summary":"The Worker demo check is not in the quality gates, and a Worker built before web/dist passes its built check while serving the old shell","supersedes":"acddd66722505cdb95b3eab866a7afdb8f2fadb62e1e960dfe592ce3e5d4bd77","tags":["demo","worker","tests","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.496808Z","id":"d0c65af3f7c5c86b1852a4fa2378dad1d4a65ec85ca2c0fcf75ad65e272d9637","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"31593a13b54c0dec306574773eeefbe84aa3e919a13e65688e6b66b626e23687","summary":"No longer reproduces at 509b1cb5: CLAX_E2E_WORKERS=1 npx playwright test e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts (fresh worker daemon, this tree's debug build) passed both modes twice (2 passed, 54.4 s with the build; 2 passed, 4.5 s). e79e7ce0 (the owner's row bumps the visibility generation once a view of who is connected was read) is the likely fix of the owner's 'Alex (not connected)' label. Proposed close: reason:fixed.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/linked.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:06:18.493147Z","id":"62d650f7b87f576a6cdef17174d714f32629536b725d42bd335a980bdff893db","body":{"detail":"target/linked-shots/ holds mirrored, pending, failed, link-row and hosted-reply shots only; the other states in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-linked-threads-design.md (UI) are covered by unit tests alone.","kind":"concern","summary":"The linked-threads browser test shoots no held thread, unlinked tag, 'on <remote> v<n>' line, inbox row or Unlink confirmation","tags":["review","linked-threads","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/db.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:36:19.553680Z","id":"d6ad2ddaf46d0a2ba97861e018eeae49e651b7d16f5bd8e7859b5cd234e4acf5","body":{"detail":"Seen under Bazel (//web:e2e_rest) once in a full run of the rest project (1 failed, 346 passed) and once in 30 runs of this test alone (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=15 --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='documents are invisible' --test_arg=e2e/db.spec.ts: 1 failed, 29 passed), always in subdomain mode. Error: frame.evaluate: CapabilityError: this document does not exist, or this viewer cannot write it, which web/shell/src/caps/db.ts:47 makes of a 404 to a write. B is named by a PUT /api/viewers/me awaited from the shell page before the write, so the server judged B's write by a viewer level from before the name, or by B's unnamed identity. The test is unchanged from main; the shell and server it drives are not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"f56b77c7f66fcb8ea00c9a3fe3e6feb386cd3b1d76ca7e37d804ac4288bce486"},"summary":"subdomain: a viewer's data/users/<id>/ documents are invisible to another viewer fails about once in thirty runs: the server answers 404 to the LAN viewer's write of its own data/users/<id>/profile right after it names itself","tags":["testing","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/db.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T07:03:04.507551Z","id":"f34ced77376746e99eed89884d796a6fcfd7ebf7ff0e8aebf19b78aa4d9b5c55","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d4643511","summary":"Fixed in d4643511. Cause: the test named B with its own PUT /api/viewers/me, sent without a cookie while the shell's first GET /api/viewers/me (also cookieless) was out; each minted a viewer and the GET's later Set-Cookie made B the unnamed one (seen in both modes, not only subdomain). An instrumented copy logged it in 2 of 200 runs under bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=100: '<- PUT 200 sentCookie=false setCookie=[clax_viewer=cxv_f6Py…] viewer=u_55ca…' then '<- GET 200 sentCookie=false setCookie=[clax_viewer=cxv_irjs…] viewer=u_eb79…', and the write as u_eb79 failed with CapabilityError. The shell's name field (NameSaver.save, web/shell/src/view/viewer-name-model.ts) saves only after that lookup answered; the test now names B there and waits for the PUT's 200. After: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=40 and then =150 --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='documents are invisible' --test_arg=e2e/db.spec.ts: 80 passed, then 300 passed.","supersedes":"d6ad2ddaf46d0a2ba97861e018eeae49e651b7d16f5bd8e7859b5cd234e4acf5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/artifact.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.360171Z","id":"96c0f3dc1012f373cc2987fbfe7fef90f4ed47c2dd7159c8a36f680c6a8d6428","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of just ci, //web:e2e_rest failed on 'sandbox: a second viewer's vote 2 s after another viewer's vote reloaded it publishes' with Error: globalThis.claxTestClock.advance(2000): TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'advance'). Rerun alone (bazel test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=...) both modes passed, and the whole e2e_rest lane alone passed (347 passed, 53 skipped). The clock was advanced in a page that had not, or no longer, loaded the test build's hook, perhaps across the reload the test makes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"f9347adb1383fec38af04c7e85bf24d13841f138772d0928f8b3cbedee679498"},"summary":"The sandbox run of \"a second viewer's vote 2 s after another viewer's vote reloaded it publishes\" failed once in just ci: the page had no test clock","tags":["tests","flaky","e2e","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:00:28.211989Z","id":"28a26f17bfcfa11fb516ecc5277d8b390e7af026ef9e5105ed912c85507ce27b","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the just ci run of 2026-10-17 at a46793c36..86a299ef4 (//web:e2e_chrome_overlay beside eleven other Bazel test actions), line 262 read window.claxHot as undefined: the page had been reloaded, not hot-updated, between the two edits of main.js. Rerun alone (bazelisk test //web:e2e_chrome_overlay '--test_arg=--grep=follow a hot reload') it passed. The branch akesling/ask-where-attention changes no dev-server, Vite or overlay reload code.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":253},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"7539cdf4836086f7efebb42b9c4e0bcdae6d9fba7a32ef84ccbe45d3f0bdd632"},"summary":"The hot-reload test can find the page fully reloaded rather than hot-updated under a loaded gate run","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:00:28.291681Z","id":"83e0a6e0eb997452a9df8e4cdda40d04bb2c8a9ed37c8b715f8722a9a2fbb0a8","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the just ci run of 2026-10-17 at 86a299ef4 (//web:e2e_chrome_overlay beside eleven other Bazel test actions), until() at line 688 threw 'timed out' waiting for the composer.html frame after the #save click; the test took 1.9 min, with launch.sh sleeping 18 s before the host starts. Rerun alone (bazelisk test //web:e2e_chrome_overlay '--test_arg=--grep=native host slow to start') it passed in 26.4 s.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":684},"end":{"line":688},"content_hash":"d896710dc4d5f39ebfc67021b64d92ecc4d11c855980db9410d4c4ea384fa7f3"},"summary":"The slow-native-host test can run out of WAIT_MS waiting for the composer frame under a loaded gate run","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:00:35.200279Z","id":"065a23271e08eaba8f879e54ee8156fd3b1139c6a7d14dbcd7874e65743b1bd8","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the just ci run of 2026-10-17 at 86a299ef4 (//web:e2e_chrome_overlay beside eleven other Bazel test actions), line 262 read window.claxHot as undefined: the page had been reloaded, not hot-updated, between the two edits of main.js. Rerun alone (bazelisk test //web:e2e_chrome_overlay '--test_arg=--grep=follow a hot reload') it passed. The branch akesling/ask-where-attention changes no dev-server, Vite or overlay reload code.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":253},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"7539cdf4836086f7efebb42b9c4e0bcdae6d9fba7a32ef84ccbe45d3f0bdd632"},"summary":"The hot-reload test can find the page fully reloaded rather than hot-updated under a loaded gate run","supersedes":"28a26f17bfcfa11fb516ecc5277d8b390e7af026ef9e5105ed912c85507ce27b","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/comment-flows.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:19:38.740726Z","id":"0db6b984f95324e22b1994b487794a0d635c519adaae6d14f77b9186f86d48d2","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the native quality-gates run of 2026-10-17 at 80549c6ec (web e2e beside cargo nextest and the other lanes), 'subdomain: flow 3, after Post, drag an area without moving first' failed at line 110: after Comment and a click on #p1 in the subdomain frame, locator('.composer .composer-quote') was not found within 5000 ms. Rerun alone (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest '--test_arg=--grep=flow 3') both modes passed in 2.4 s. The branch akesling/ask-where-attention changes no composer, picker, gesture or frame code (git diff aa0696af3..HEAD --stat -- web/ lists none).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"fae3f57df57441cea02a1ce1283fd639f945e2d95f7631901b9dbac1df6e27ee"},"summary":"The subdomain flow-3 test's first pick can find no composer under a loaded gate run","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005154Z","id":"bdb345cbe43d326414c751adf197c87d0bf5ecfbafff8869d8d9464acab3e080","body":{"detail":"Failure: any //web:e2e_chrome_overlay test whose page is open when the late event arrives; under a busy fseventsd (load average 4 to 8) it broke a different set of tests each run. In 3 runs of bazelisk test //web:e2e_chrome_overlay with the fixture logging site.watcher 'all' events (2 at 4ffb96fbf, 1 at 641706256), every fixture's Vite watcher reported 'change' for the copied index.html and main.js 0.5 s to 10.9 s after its 'ready', all workers' events arriving at the same instant. The files had not been written since cpSync. Vite answers an index.html change with a full reload of the open page, which drops the page's window state and can land mid-test. At 4ffb96fbf the suite failed in 3 of 7 runs (chrome-overlay.spec.ts:169, :314, :666, :1065); at 641706256 in 7 of 9 (:169, :666, :697, :950). Waiting for 'ready' (line 201) does not wait for those events.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"d01aad585d0b6690cc760cd668f3a02661c3d05eef7f56fc80e6f64a7c17f792"},"suggested_fix":"Copy the site, then wait until the watcher has been quiet for the copied paths (or drop events whose file content matches the copy) before opening a page; or ignore the copy's events by comparing mtimes to the copy time.","summary":"FSEvents can report the live site's copied files as changed seconds after Vite's watcher is ready, and Vite then fully reloads the test's page","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005248Z","id":"2ef8e373334dc7a6f48a2b755e73f90e1aad2f2d2f1fc99733916921a048a927","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'Clax is on only in the tab it was turned on in…' (seen at 4ffb96fbf and in an earlier gate run) failed in a //web:e2e_chrome_overlay run beside the suite's other tests and passed in others, at 4ffb96fbf and at 641706256 alike. Cause recorded on web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts:192:201: a spurious index.html change event seconds after the watcher's ready makes Vite reload the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":314},"content_hash":"e45471e3237abde49a2f6dfdcfb0e5157b5e5499f751724b1c6ee9f7a0724bbb"},"summary":"The test at line 314 can fail when Vite fully reloads its page on a late FSEvents report of the copied live site","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
