{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:08:29.107292Z","id":"eda8ec2e19b1080c8ded320310ae51a754e21fa469722ce700aa91f9c9b0f74a","body":{"detail":"Passed 5 of 5 alone. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"4b2e54f93bea887975ed8ca10f6ce06c75a80510dc194e3dea17d29c3ddf1db6"},"summary":"'the artifact deleted while the viewer types in it leaves the keyboard free' took 6.2 min in one gates run","supersedes":"5cfcbebcab703a3b4870ddeea008d1500403828dff957097ffddfc90ef323a60","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598645Z","id":"65c68033f882683e2c27e069e35b91b95cb96fb873d38681b225a40da114707b","body":{"detail":"The e2e specs check a tag by keyboard and click and close the editor with Escape. Nothing checks: a refused PATCH (too_many_tags past 20, or admin_only) showing its message and unchecking the box; a press outside or focus leaving closing the popover (ui/tag-editor.ts:45-55); the editor closing when the view ends or the viewer loses may_tag (tag-editor.ts:49). tag-picker.test.ts covers TagPicker with a stub onToggle only; TagEditor.svelte has no test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"1cd70e51a66a9bca34564e28e9aa3969833534b77b509e024240f2619cb50e33"},"suggested_fix":"Add a tags.spec.ts case that applies 20 tags by API and checks a 21st in the editor (alert text, box unchecked), and one that presses outside and tabs out; add a TagEditor unit test with a held PATCH.","summary":"No test covers the tag editor's refusal, the twenty-tag limit, or its popover closing paths","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","tests","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.413479Z","id":"dd77e260972809c3b395e31ecb0c755883e70d48b51ed0a1ead805c6e6d04d1d","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts has five tests (lines 25, 109, 146, 164, 193); the editor case closes only with Escape (line 68). `grep -rln \"too_many_tags\\|TagEditor\\|tag-pop\" web/e2e web/shell/src` matches no test file (only .qual files, web/shell/src/artifact.ts and the components themselves). The untested close paths are web/shell/src/ui/tag-editor.ts:43 (pointerdown outside), :48 (state subscription on dispose / button disconnect) and :49-52 (focusout).","kind":"comment","references":"65c68033f882683e2c27e069e35b91b95cb96fb873d38681b225a40da114707b","summary":"confirmed: no test exercises the tag editor's refusal, the twenty-tag limit, or its outside-press/focus-out/view-end close paths","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.967090Z","id":"c868966943e5898b231bfbbb7193e8ce5b283b0c66a045c0c477666200cd54df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3113e2aed","summary":"Fixed: tags.spec.ts 'the tag editor shows a refusal past twenty tags…' checks a 21st tag's message and unchecked box and a press outside closing the editor; tag-editor.test.ts unit-tests TagEditor (order, refusal) and the popover closing on a press outside, focus leaving, Escape and the view ending or its button going (//web:unit passes; //web:e2e_rest tags.spec.ts inbox.spec.ts: 8 passed)","supersedes":"65c68033f882683e2c27e069e35b91b95cb96fb873d38681b225a40da114707b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:43:10.915052Z","id":"7382322766e2144d88b140e7fd8bfa7fd0b6a415bc25d1bfa8fa97a8deed1ac0","body":{"detail":"Under a machine load average of about 90 on 12 cores, `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest` with --grep for both tests and --repeat-each=10 passed all 60 runs (both modes, both key spacings). The failing run's output was not kept, so the failing assertion is unknown. Candidates: typeOn with spacing 0 queues every key while a Tab out of a cross-origin frame moves focus across processes, so a key routed to the frame before focus lands shifts the walk and the Space misses Send (the act-hint check at line 382); or the 5 s expect timeout on the pin or hint.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"ee819237803576b9feffc002d06c5e8f869fe405a08d7de2a4d3e31baa0c0fee"},"summary":"The subdomain variants of this test and of the one at line 405 failed under load in a gates run and were not reproduced","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/gesture.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:46:40.950981Z","id":"c60ce6267cbe1133e4b30f238fc1f0bf10b4d33a221cf36d60e3971716eb3051","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aff36e5dd","summary":"activationLapsed (web/e2e/time.ts) no longer gives up after 10 s, and the gesture project's timeout is 90 s. Evidence: bazelisk test //web:e2e_gesture --test_arg=e2e/gesture.spec.ts --test_arg=--grep=N14 --test_arg=--repeat-each=10 passed 120 of 120 at a load average of about 90 on 12 cores (slowest 12.3 s).","supersedes":"2c771fe38d3d0645ca5e87c1cabe0466ddc9ecbf9298c9257e4b5441eabf38d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/owner.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.756260Z","id":"343d7934ee148e517bc244dd7069f0374c70cf11abbb1da783a185519ea9142a","body":{"detail":"Failure: GitHub CI run 39440289806 (Linux, //web:e2e_rest, 8 workers): after setName(chrome, \"Alex\") and the safari field showing Alex, the LAN viewer's People and agents dialog had 0 .prow rows containing Alex (13 polls over 5000 ms). The other runs passed. The CI log has no trace or page state, so it does not show whether the rename event never reached the LAN viewer's page or reached it late; not investigated further.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"4528bdb052fc8e3b696fadd18fb236e3bfde096ccc35206b01c517bce162e7e4"},"summary":"The LAN viewer's roster did not show the owner's new name within 5 s once in CI","tags":["tests","flaky","e2e","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:59:23.786760Z","id":"9151ba2de305d4a97a4fb5e72a2b2c8b82b6ec791e336aacdf621260fa8a325e","body":{"detail":"Under load the LAN viewer's click on Add sometimes adds nothing: the daemon holds only 'Seeded one', the page still shows 'add invalid_argument' from the refusal before naming, and the title field still holds 'From the LAN'. That is either a click that never reached the form or an add refused again. Ruled out: the viewer's level is computed per request (crates/clax-http/src/db_caller.rs base_caller); the db capability does not narrow it; the rename does not reload the capability host. The pointer-reach change in web/e2e/fixtures.ts (6da3a3c9d) did not stop it (1 failure in 3 full-suite runs). Next: log the frame's submit/pointerdown events beside the /docs requests and their statuses. Re-enable once fixed; it covers a LAN viewer's write level.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"c32515fd370ab8de40ccf3b4c8e748f38c2a789a3c4d4274ff7df9c912cbbef8"},"summary":"LAN tracker test skipped (test.fixme) while it flakes under load","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:59:23.996246Z","id":"4801a7663df4428f43434a51ec0ffc73b4dff4db3ff7007a03a28a8b3290b455","body":{"detail":"The test presses Tab 12 times from the pin and expects Send focused. With all chrome mounted there are 13 stops (12 Tabs after the pin); on a loaded machine one lazily mounted control can arrive late, so the presses stop short. The sibling test near line 368 types a fixed 13-Tab sequence and depends on the same count. A fix that waited for the 13 stops before clicking into the page passed 4/4 targeted and 6/6 full-suite runs but was not proven at 10 repeats. Fix: wait for the chrome that adds stops, or Tab until Send has focus with a bound; then drop the test.fixme.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":421},"content_hash":"b8175a55701a13ed8ca1dd5946e39e4e0473f6c4702ea2ffd30104b625f71359"},"summary":"Keyboard-send test skipped in subdomain mode while a fixed Tab count misses Send","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:44.888752Z","id":"ed55a45fe5e5a8358f7569ff3451473a26e06b44ded33964759dc6e4f76b3147","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:06f59eb43","summary":"Fixed in 06f59eb43: the late stop is the New comment box (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte imports NewComment.svelte apart). Holding its chunk (page.route on NewComment-*.js) put Send 11 stops from the pin and twelve Tabs passed it, in both modes. The test now waits until tabsFromPin(Send) is 12 (web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts:354) and runs in subdomain mode again. Beside 36 busy loops: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=60 --test_arg=--grep for this test, the other keyboard tests, attention.spec.ts and owner.spec.ts: 720 passed, 0 failed (60 per test and mode).","supersedes":"4801a7663df4428f43434a51ec0ffc73b4dff4db3ff7007a03a28a8b3290b455","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/owner.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:45.273941Z","id":"a5c66ac4d1b4885f3e0afc5bd5773201046f4244f1390762257619dd910ecfd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:90b8221e4","summary":"Fixed in 90b8221e4. Cause: a presence answer replaced the view's list even when a presence event had arrived since its request started. The LAN viewer's refetch on its stream's reconnect (after it names itself Mia) could be answered after the owner's rename event, putting the owner back unnamed: an e2e experiment holding that GET /api/artifacts/<id>/presence until the rename showed in the LAN roster, then delivering it, removed the Alex row in 3 of 3 runs before the fix and kept it in 5 of 5 after. web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.test.ts 'a presence answer to a request made before a presence event ...' fails without the ticket check ('expected 0 to be greater than 0') and passes with it. owner.spec.ts beside 36 busy loops: 120 of 120 passed (two --repeat-each=60 runs).","supersedes":"343d7934ee148e517bc244dd7069f0374c70cf11abbb1da783a185519ea9142a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:45.800375Z","id":"ef7f7ab7207af6acec1606e750bd6dcfaadc18366a6207ec9d9360dd3462e41e","body":{"detail":"Under a machine load average of about 90 on 12 cores, `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest` with --grep for both tests and --repeat-each=10 passed all 60 runs (both modes, both key spacings). The failing run's output was not kept, so the failing assertion is unknown. Candidates: typeOn with spacing 0 queues every key while a Tab out of a cross-origin frame moves focus across processes, so a key routed to the frame before focus lands shifts the walk and the Space misses Send (the act-hint check); or a Tab stop that mounts late. The second is now ruled out for this test: the New comment box loads in its own chunk, and with that chunk held Send is 11 stops from the pin, so this walk's Space misses Send; since 06f59eb43 the test waits for 12 stops first. After that, beside 36 busy loops, --repeat-each=60 twice passed 120 of 120 per mode for this test and for the line-418 test in both spacings. Close once a gates run passes them, or record the failing assertion if one recurs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":396},"content_hash":"79786f2aa44348beaff726a8eeb1776a265d703c1a5433aedfe50e7aebfc32c7"},"summary":"The subdomain variants of this test and of the one at line 418 failed under load in a gates run and were not reproduced","supersedes":"7382322766e2144d88b140e7fd8bfa7fd0b6a415bc25d1bfa8fa97a8deed1ac0","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:46.444968Z","id":"8e2c7500ab49106afb7a0468cf750bbf2217562cbbf628c2c01414fdc6e7d0b1","body":{"detail":"Passed 5 of 5 alone. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":458},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"4b2e54f93bea887975ed8ca10f6ce06c75a80510dc194e3dea17d29c3ddf1db6"},"summary":"'the artifact deleted while the viewer types in it leaves the keyboard free' took 6.2 min in one gates run","supersedes":"eda8ec2e19b1080c8ded320310ae51a754e21fa469722ce700aa91f9c9b0f74a","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:47.015933Z","id":"dcffad35308977976745de57d02dbe41fdd9568788927ceaf22733b8186a6e8f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9151ba2de305d4a97a4fb5e72a2b2c8b82b6ec791e336aacdf621260fa8a325e","summary":"Not reproduced, so still skipped. Unskipped, it passed 200 of 200 runs beside 36 busy loops (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=200 --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='LAN: the tracker') and 3 of 3 in one run of the whole rest project with --repeat-each=3 beside 12 busy loops. One reading of the failure narrows it: before naming, the test's #save-note click set the status to 'note invalid_argument', so a status of 'add invalid_argument' after naming means the post-naming Add was submitted and refused again, not lost to a shield band or a missed click. Look next at which viewer that PUT /api/artifacts/<id>/docs/tasks/<id> carried and the level base_caller (crates/clax-http/src/db_caller.rs:72) gave it; a trace of a passing run shows one viewer cookie throughout and the add answered 200 right after the name's PUT. Two other flakes found here were orderings the test did not wait for (records 343d7934 and 4801a766).","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
